// The domestic water supply, in building coordinates: the 3/4 in PEX service from under the slab, the
// 50 gal electric water heater, the home-run PEX manifold, and 1/2 in PEX hot and cold runs to
// the washer box and the kitchen sink, routed through bored I-joist webs and LVL beams.
// Four 1/2 in home runs from the manifold to the second-floor baths (hall cold and hot,
// primary cold and hot). They rise beside the manifold into the floor joist space, cross beams B and C
// in bored holes (middle third, at x = 25'-9 1/2" to 26'-5"), and branch in bay C-D to each fixture:
// stubs up through the floor at the toilets and vanities, risers in the partition between the baths
// for the shower valve, and in wall D for the tub valve.
